--
-- The phone's database is two files' worth of schema:
--
--   Replica.sq — what a person said: every synced row, merged by field
--                (spec/sync.yaml). The only copy of an unpushed edit.
--   Local.sq   — what this phone derived from its FIT files. Rebuilt from
--                the files, never synced.
--
-- This file used to hold the server mirror (activity/daily_metric tables fed
-- by /sync/delta), the cached_document store and the outbox. All three went
-- with the move to a phone that works without a server; see
-- docs/offline-first.md. It stays as the database's named entry point.
--
-- No migrations: a schema change drops everything and resyncs (see
-- TracksSchema), which is acceptable only while nobody but the developer
-- depends on this app.

-- SQLDelight needs at least one statement per file.
schemaNote:
SELECT 1;
